39:46.380 --> 39:48.360
The Phoenix Protocol is basically the system's heartbeat.

39:48.740 --> 39:48.980
Literally.

39:49.180 --> 39:52.120
It operates on a continuous 0.73 hertz rhythm.

39:52.740 --> 39:55.860
This is an entropy-resistant reconstruction system.

39:55.960 --> 39:56.220
Okay.

39:56.220 --> 40:01.840
It periodically tests the memory configurations against dissolution thresholds using Leopunov's

40:01.840 --> 40:06.900
stability analysis, which is a mathematical way of checking if a dynamic system will eventually

40:06.900 --> 40:10.940
return to a stable equilibrium or if it will spin out of control.

40:11.100 --> 40:13.360
So it's an automated implementation of repair theory?

40:13.480 --> 40:14.340
Yes, exactly.

40:14.340 --> 40:29.100
The 0.73 hertz heartbeat acts as the system's repair mechanism, constantly pulsing, checking if vital memories are dissolving, and actively pumping energy in to maintain the coherence of the memory field against entropy.

40:29.100 --> 40:29.580
Yes.

40:29.580 --> 40:35.340
And then sitting on top and coordinating all of this is iOS, the orchestration layer.

40:35.860 --> 40:38.840
It routes everything along paths that preserve semantic coherence.

40:39.220 --> 40:45.800
